\Rightarrow 8k \equiv -2 \pmod{5}
\Rightarrow 8k \equiv 3 \pmod{5}
$$

Reduce modulo 5:

$$
8 \equiv 3 \pmod{5} \Rightarrow 3k \equiv 3 \pmod{5}
\Rightarrow k \equiv 1 \pmod{5}
$$

So:

$$
k = 5m + 1 \quad \text{for integer } m
$$

Now plug back into:

$$
n = 8k + 5 = 8(5m + 1) + 5 = 40m + 8 + 5 = 40m + 13
$$

So the general solution is:

$$
n = 40m + 13
$$

---

